{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1164927-influence-of-summoning-supernal-beings","id":1164927,"title":"Influence of Summoning Supernal Beings","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-03T17:31:19-08:00","id":1164927,"title":"Influence of Summoning Supernal Beings","content":"Hey Everyone,<br /> <br /> So, I was reading over the Summoning Supernal Entities section in the Mage the Awakening Book and noticed in the Ephemeral Entities section regarding Influence &amp; Arcana the following statement:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> a Supernal being possesses dots in two Arcana equal to its Rank, one of which must be one of the Ruling Arcana of its Realm, and may have additional Arcana at lower ratings. </div> </div> </div>So, this is a little confusing to me, so let me throw down a scenario for you and let me know:<br /> A Moros decides to summon a Rank 3 Supernal Entity and they chose the Recondite with Life as the secondary Arcana, which means this would be a Death 2 Life 1 or Death 1 Life 2 Supernal Being, correct?<br /> Or would it be a Death 3 Life 3 Supernal Being?<br /> <br /> If it is the former, it would logically mean you have to summon a Rank 6 being to get a Death 5 Supernal Being. Which, would be impossible since Mages cannot summon beings greater than Rank 5. I imagine it is the latter, but it also raises the question about how you decide the additional Arcana at lower ratings since it seems it has a number of dots equal to its Rank in two Arcana and without Numina they can't trade it for additional influence.<br /> <br /> Let me know if I am understanding correctly, thanks in advance! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T17:51:14-08:00","id":1164935,"title":"","content":"If you summoned a rank 3 Supernal entity with Death as its primary arcana then it would appear with Death 3, and if you targeted it to have Life it would also have Life 3, and it might have other arcana at 2 or 1 dots and whether or not it would have these additional arcana is entirely up to the ST. That's how I read it anyway.<br /> <br /> Edit: Supernal entities are by far more difficult to come by than any other kind of entity that might be entreated for assistance, so it makes sense there would be a commensurate power boost to make it worthwhile. Also, even once successfully summoned they have some kind of esoteric trial to overcome before you can actually sit down and ask them for help, and that trial gets increasingly more difficult the higher their Rank. So really, before you can do anything with a Supernal Entity you have to clear two hurdles.<br /> <br /> The one exception is when a Mage accidentally summons a Supernal Entity via a dramatic failure with their Scrutiny rolls, in which case there are other attendant dangers to be dealt with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 12-03-2017, 08:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T02:50:39-08:00","id":1165262,"title":"","content":"Honestly, with the way supernal entities are implemented in the core book, they're a bit lackluster. At best they can give you advice you might not find somewhere else. But apparently in 1e, there were rules released that give Supernal Entities unique powers called Boons(?). I think they will be in Signs of Sorcery. Personally as an ST I would sort of wing it with Supernal Entities and give them unique powers that could benefit the mage, aside from their Arcana. This gives a reason for a mage to seek out an Entity rather than rolling down to the local Consilium and finding a probably much-less-dangerous mage who has the Arcana they need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T08:05:29-08:00","id":1165310,"title":"","content":"you have to actually have the secondary arcana at 3+ to select it as secondary for the summoned creature<br /> but hey, a Death 3\\Matter 3 Moros could summon a Death 5\\Matter 5 Shade","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1djeav1YTEwQq1fkDtWEKh7PPVFmzj3y-\" target=\"_blank\">The Repository</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13158-sir-bardiel","name":"Sir Bardiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13158_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T09:27:11-08:00","id":1165334,"title":"","content":"Something which is clear in the Supernal Entities section, but not in the Targeted Summoning Attainment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T09:34:30-08:00","id":1165337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1164927-influence-of-summoning-supernal-beings?p=1165334#post1165334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something which is clear in the Supernal Entities section, but not in the Targeted Summoning Attainment.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s because the attainment refers you directly to the section on summoning Supernal entities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T10:52:54-08:00","id":1165364,"title":"","content":"It's still written wrong though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T11:27:44-08:00","id":1165373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1164927-influence-of-summoning-supernal-beings?p=1165364#post1165364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's still written wrong though.</div> </div> </div> </div>In what way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T13:37:45-08:00","id":1165408,"title":"","content":"&quot;Targeted Summoning<br /> <br /> With three dots in an Arcanum, a mage can add greater specificity when summoning a Supernal being (p. 94). All Supernal beings have a primary Arcanum, defined by their<br /> home Realm and the type of being (manifest or recondite). They can have other Arcana, however, and a mage using this Attainment can narrow her summoning to Supernal beings with particular powers. System: The mage spends one additional Mana during the summoning, and specifies a second Arcanum for the target Supernal being. The primary Arcanum must remain one of the mage\u2019s two Path Ruling Arcana.&quot;<br /> <br /> Nowhere does it say which Arcana needs to have 3 dots, the Primary or the Secondary. It's sloppy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T13:43:12-08:00","id":1165411,"title":"","content":"First of all, the primary arcana obviously has to have 3 dots or you can\u2019t even use the attainment. Second of all it\u2019s made clear in the Supernal entity summoning rules which are referenced before the text that you quoted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T13:47:39-08:00","id":1165412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1164927-influence-of-summoning-supernal-beings?p=1165408#post1165408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;Targeted Summoning<br /> <br /> With three dots in an Arcanum, a mage can add greater specificity when summoning a Supernal being (p. 94). All Supernal beings have a primary Arcanum, defined by their<br /> home Realm and the type of being (manifest or recondite). They can have other Arcana, however, and a mage using this Attainment can narrow her summoning to Supernal beings with particular powers. System: The mage spends one additional Mana during the summoning, and specifies a second Arcanum for the target Supernal being. The primary Arcanum must remain one of the mage\u2019s two Path Ruling Arcana.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Nowhere does it say which Arcana needs to have 3 dots, the Primary or the Secondary. It's sloppy.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does by implication, doesn\u2019t it? Otherwise, why mention \u2018other Arcana\u2019 in the first place?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T14:52:26-08:00","id":1165433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1164927-influence-of-summoning-supernal-beings?p=1165411#post1165411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all, the primary arcana obviously has to have 3 dots or you can\u2019t even use the attainment. Second of all it\u2019s made clear in the Supernal entity summoning rules which are referenced before the text that you quoted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I think if you have death 3 matter 2 and mind 3 you can summon a matter 3 mind 3 rank 3 supernal entity","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T15:00:19-08:00","id":1165437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1164927-influence-of-summoning-supernal-beings?p=1165433#post1165433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually I think if you have death 3 matter 2 and mind 3 you can summon a matter 3 mind 3 rank 3 supernal entity</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No. I see how you could read the rules that way, but you'd have to all but be intentionally trying to break them not to get the drift in a section that requires you to have an Arcana 3 to use. <br /> <br /> ******<br /> <br /> In regards to: Supernal Entities=Lackluster, there's a few things. First, they can bring Artifacts. Second, they have knowledge and information, often, that cannot be obtained easily. They're beings from a Realm that's positively platonic. If you can't find interesting knowledge for a Supernal Entity to have, then you aren't thinking hard enough. <br /> <br /> Finally, by the way. Supernal Entities have Infinite Free Reach. I think that a clever ST could easily think of impossible-for-Mages Reach conditions for certain spells to make them fundamentally better or more powerful than anything a non-Archmage can do. At the very least, they'd probably never struggle to cast spells with truly outrageous durations and that are really hard to undo, and they might also know how to do things with magic that few can do. I mean, a Mind 5, Space 5, Life 4 entity (Rank 5) might have some crazy, insane combo of conjoining spells/effects. Basically, and this is certainly something they could firm up at a later date so that it's not wide open, the sky's the limit if you're a creative ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12866-the_laurent","name":"The_Laurent","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T15:02:32-08:00","id":1165438,"title":"","content":"Sorry but I disagree. You do have one at 3: Mind. I still don't think its clear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T15:06:47-08:00","id":1165439,"title":"","content":"You need 3 dots in the Ruling Arcanum you use to Summon, so no. You could summon a Shade with Mind as its secondary for a mana, though.<br /> <br /> EDIT: You can only summon Supernal beings from your Realm. To do so you need to use one of the Ruling Arcanum of that Realm. You need that Arcanum at least at 3 dots. How is it not clear that you cannot summon a Shade with Mind 3?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 12-05-2017, 06:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T15:20:57-08:00","id":1165442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1164927-influence-of-summoning-supernal-beings?p=1165438#post1165438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry but I disagree. You do have one at 3: Mind. I still don't think its clear.</div> </div> </div> </div>The very rules you quoted clearly state that the primary arcana (You know, the one being used to activate the attainment) must be one of your Ruling arcana. Matter 2, Mind 3 would fail if you\u2019re a Moros.<br /> <br /> The exception is when you pick up a third ruling arcana from a legacy. If your hypothetical Moros was initiated into a legacy with Mind primary it would work, -but- to specifically request an entity that has Matter as a secondary arcana it would require that you have Matter 3 as detailed on pg. 94 where the rules tell you quite clearly to check.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T15:22:46-08:00","id":1165444,"title":"","content":"OK. I missed where it said that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T07:22:58-08:00","id":1165865,"title":"","content":"I think there's other things being missed here. The entity can cast spells for you that you don't have to maintain, and spell-control is kinda tight in this game. Furthermore they can, as some people said, cast things that no mere mage could and that's not just relevant at high levels.<br /> <br /> For example, a Rank 3 with Prime could cast Super Vision on you with indef duration and every imaginable sort of reach effect applied to it. Want to be able to get the info reflexively instead of after a turns study? Done. Enemies insist on trying to dispel your spells before a fight? Advanced potency. Strange supernaturals hide among the population? Done, you can now identify them. Don't think the normal spell gives enough info? Well, Supernal entity you just summoned has -infinitely- more experience with it than you and has a +3 Reach effect applied that just goes towards giving more info.<br /> <br /> Or maybe all of the above is irrelevant, you just want to find those damn Strix and give them whatsfor? Well, the spirit knows a +2 Reach effect that is an upgrade to the one in the book, allowing you to narrow the vision to only the aura's of those possessed by Strix. Now you can pick them out of crowds easy peasy and also study their auras with no issue.<br /> <br /> In short even low level spells, when cast with that much freedom, can do truly fantastic things and these beings have all the knowledge of those fantastic things you could possibly dream of. Don't dismiss them because they can't necessarily cast spells you can't; keep in mind that they can still be FAR better at those spells than you! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T10:52:04-08:00","id":1165897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asaram</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1164927-influence-of-summoning-supernal-beings?p=1165865#post1165865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there's other things being missed here. The entity can cast spells for you that you don't have to maintain, and spell-control is kinda tight in this game. Furthermore they can, as some people said, cast things that no mere mage could and that's not just relevant at high levels.<br /> <br /> For example, a Rank 3 with Prime could cast Super Vision on you with indef duration and every imaginable sort of reach effect applied to it. Want to be able to get the info reflexively instead of after a turns study? Done. Enemies insist on trying to dispel your spells before a fight? Advanced potency. Strange supernaturals hide among the population? Done, you can now identify them. Don't think the normal spell gives enough info? Well, Supernal entity you just summoned has -infinitely- more experience with it than you and has a +3 Reach effect applied that just goes towards giving more info.<br /> <br /> Or maybe all of the above is irrelevant, you just want to find those damn Strix and give them whatsfor? Well, the spirit knows a +2 Reach effect that is an upgrade to the one in the book, allowing you to narrow the vision to only the aura's of those possessed by Strix. Now you can pick them out of crowds easy peasy and also study their auras with no issue.<br /> <br /> In short even low level spells, when cast with that much freedom, can do truly fantastic things and these beings have all the knowledge of those fantastic things you could possibly dream of. Don't dismiss them because they can't necessarily cast spells you can't; keep in mind that they can still be FAR better at those spells than you! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's homebrew. Not disaggreeing here with the concept, but if such reach options are allowed a mage should be able to utilize them too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T13:37:40-08:00","id":1165934,"title":"","content":"They could be, yes, and in most cases should be able to provided they know enough about strix to make such a thing work. The point here is that these entities know more about all low level spells than mages because they are part of the supernal and can use it with such finesse that Reach isn't even limited to them.<br /> <br /> At three dots a mage could cast such a spell as Prolonged, Instant and with the original Reach option without over-reaching. For these entities casting it on you with those things, Indefinite duration, Advanced Potency and even more Reach options to refine things is still perfectly doable and provokes absolutely no paradox. In short, even if you already have the spell you can benefit immensely from Supernal Summoning, provided you're willing to take what risks are associated with it and end up with a creature willing to help.<br /> <br /> And it's also worth noting, it could do the exact same thing with a third-dot spell as a one-dot one, and there the example character only has one reach... the contrast and possible benefits grows even more clear. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}